{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1447712-6-holdings","id":1447712,"title":"+6 Holdings?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-06T07:40:42-07:00","id":1447712,"title":"+6 Holdings?","content":"Now that Holdings have a point system, how would you go about getting a Freehold that gives the 5 points of glamour, is the size of a small town (because it IS a small, rural town down in Texas that you have revitalized) and has Sanctum 5 (must keep the Balefire and people safe) plus the additional benefits like glamour to dross and multiple archetypes. Can you make a Freehold that strong? It lists trods as a Holding background, and you can make those with heroic effort, so what of the other benefits?<br /> <br /> Perhaps sacrificing multiple treasures when making the Freehold, or + 6 dots Glamour being sacrificed when creating the Freehold?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 05-06-2021, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T13:51:26-07:00","id":1448459,"title":"","content":"I don't think the amount of dots in the freehold background has any correlation to it's size. A freehold that produces 1 point of glamour could be a castle, and a freehold that produces 5 could be a castle too... or a small secret house in the middle of the city. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> About level 6 freeholds, I would avoid it, not because it's &quot;too powerful&quot; but simply to avoid making uncessary rules about that. If it's something done throught roleplay during the chronicle, then the level of power doesn't matter, go for a freehold that produces 6 glamour points, or 10, or one that varies chaotically, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But one idea that I could suggest is making a freehold that used to have a grand balefire (like the one in Tara-nar) as a justification for why it's so much stronger, lore wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:41:27-07:00","id":1449938,"title":"","content":"Mercurial is referring to the rules in the Book of Freeholds, which allow you to allocate points in several different characteristics for your freehold. You could even make it produce less glamour than its rating would suggest, instead making it a nexus for trods to all sorts of locations...<br /> <br /> That said, i think a freehold that exceeds the 6+ rating should be something only gained through story, and not bought with freebies.<br /> Also... it would attract attention from other Fae who believe you not to be &quot;worthy&quot; of such a place, of Prodigals who want to take over the place, and possibly of hunters who know enough about ley lines that they suspect the place to be a hiding hole for evil creatures...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}